# Forge API conventions

Adapted from `/home/c7d5a6/projects/rts/c7d5a6l/.cursor/rules/backend-go.mdc` so both projects read the same way. This rule covers **architecture**; code style lives in `go-style.mdc` and `Style.md`.

Full write-up: `packages/forge/api/README.md`. Schema: `docs/forge/schema.md`.

## Layers

| Package | Role |
|---|---|
| `internal/handler` | HTTP only (prefer this name over "controller") |
| `internal/service` | Business use-cases; **TX for any DB writes** |
| `internal/repository` | All SQLite access, via sqlc-generated code |
| `internal/model` | Domain types. No behaviour, no imports from this module |
| `internal/db` | Connection setup, pragmas, migration runner |
| `internal/export` | YAML, JSON, and Markdown emitters |

Dependency flow: `handler → service → repository`. One direction.

## Rules

1. Handlers do not run SQL and do not open transactions. Decode, validate shape, call one service, encode.
2. Service methods that write: `BeginTx` → work → `Commit`, with `defer Rollback()`.
3. `internal/model` imports nothing from this module. It is the tygo input, and a dependency there leaks into generated TypeScript.
4. `internal/export` reads; it never writes to the database. Export is one-way by design — see `docs/forge/export-formats.md`.
5. No hand-written SQL strings and no query builders. Queries live in `query/*.sql` and go through `sqlc`, which type-checks them against `migrations/`.
6. Generated code (`internal/repository/generated/`, `packages/shared/src/generated/`) is gitignored and never hand-edited. Regenerate with `pnpm forge:sqlc` / `pnpm forge:types`.
7. `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` on every connection. Without it SQLite silently ignores foreign keys, which defeats the relational schema.
8. Handlers are a **boundary**: log and return a status, never panic. Keep recover middleware installed in `cmd/forge`.
9. `net/http` with `ServeMux` method-and-path patterns. No router framework — there are a few dozen routes.
10. The committed database is `packages/content/content.sqlite`. Tests copy fixtures to a temp file per test; never write a committed database from a test.
11. Validate before export and report **every** problem at once. Fixing content one error per run is miserable — see the validation list in `docs/forge/export-formats.md`.

## Identity

`id`, `slug`, and `foundry_id` are identity and never change: no regeneration on export, no rewriting in a migration. `label` is the mutable human-readable field. Conflating identity with display name is the specific mistake CoC7, WFRP4e, and SWFFG all made (`docs/research/04-skill-systems.md`).
